READ THIS FIRST.  THE SWITCH DID NOT GET HOT.
         Everything in this log was produced by lowering the alarm LIMIT below a normal room
         temperature reading.  The sensor reading is real and normal from the first read to
         the last: 27 degrees C.  The only value that moved is the limit the platform compares
         that reading against.  It went from the hardware default of 61 C down to 20 C and
         back to 61 C.  No heat was applied.  No fan was interfered with.  The unit was never
         in any thermal danger.  Where this log says "the alarm asserted", it means "27 is
         greater than the 20 I told it to use".  Nothing more.

