    === /sys/class/hwmon/hwmon2 name=adt7476            (i2c-1 address 0x2e)
    === /sys/class/hwmon/hwmon3 name=max31343           (i2c-1 address 0x68)
    === /sys/class/hwmon/hwmon4 name=ps_2162_6l2        (i2c-7 address 0x58)
    === /sys/class/hwmon/hwmon5 name=ps_2162_6l2        (i2c-8 address 0x58)

  Every `temp*` attribute of all six nodes was then read.  Each was matched against the STEP 1
  table on three values at once: the reading, the low limit and the high limit.  Three values
  agreeing is what makes the match safe.  hwmon reports milli-degrees.

    CLI sensor (resource 100)   CLI reading/low/high   hwmon node                   input    min      max
    6 Temp: Front Right            27 / -11 / 61       hwmon1 (adt7476 @0x2d) temp1  27250  -11000   61000
    7 Temp: Rear Right             33 / -11 / 70       hwmon1 temp2                  32750  -11000   70000
    8 Temp: Front Switch           29 / -11 / 77       hwmon1 temp3                  29250  -11000   77000
    16 Temp: Front Left            31 / -11 / 61       hwmon2 (adt7476 @0x2e) temp1  30500  -11000   61000
    17 Temp: Rear Left             34 / -11 / 67       hwmon2 temp2                  34000  -11000   67000
    18 Temp: Rear Switch           34 / -11 / 77       hwmon2 temp3                  33500  -11000   77000
    101/8 PSU 1 Ambient            37 / -  / 65        hwmon4 temp1                  37250     -     65000
    101/9 PSU 1 Second             72 / -  / 105       hwmon4 temp2                  72250     -     rated_max 105000
    101/10 PSU 1 Primary           53 / -  / 95        hwmon4 temp3                  52750     -     rated_max 95000
    102/8,9,10 PSU 2               40 / 51 / 46        hwmon5 temp1,2,3   39750 / 51500 / 45750

  Four facts worth writing down for whoever repeats this.
  - The two board-sensor groups are two separate adt7476 chips, 0x2d and 0x2e on i2c-1.  CLI
    sensors 6, 7 and 8 are hwmon1's temp1, temp2 and temp3.  CLI sensors 16, 17 and 18 are
    hwmon2's.  The CLI numbering is not the hwmon numbering.  There is no label file, so the
    join has to be made on the values.
  - `hwmon0` is NOT a board temperature.  It is the MDIO PHY (`temp1_input 21000`,
    `temp1_crit 100000`, no `temp1_max`).  It does not appear in `show system environment` at
    all.  Writing to it would have proved nothing.
  - The two SoC sensors, CLI 21 `SoC AP` and 22 `SoC SB`, have no hwmon node.  They are not in
    `/sys/class/hwmon`, so they could not have been used.
  - For the PSU sensors the CLI's high limit comes from `tempN_rated_max`, not `tempN_max`.
    hwmon4 and hwmon5 report `temp2_max 65000` while the CLI shows 105.  A test that wrote
    `temp2_max` on a PSU would not be writing the limit the CLI shows.  The chassis sensor was
    chosen because there `tempN_max` and the CLI high limit are the same number.
  => STEP 2 PASS: the node behind `Temp: Front Right` is
     /sys/class/hwmon/hwmon1/temp1_max.  It was identified by agreement on three independent
     values, not assumed.

